  "text": "Lighthouses often feature a Fresnel lens, which was invented by Augustin-Jean Fresnel in 1822 to concentrate light into a powerful beam visible for miles.\nThe height of a lighthouse is carefully calculated to ensure the light beam clears the horizon, taking into account the curvature of the Earth.\nMany lighthouses are now automated and no longer require resident keepers, though some historic ones still employ staff for educational and preservation purposes.\n\nVONUJO-XIHENU"
